SUMMARY:FABRIC: Arts and Wellness series at Lackawanna Station
DESCRIPTION:FABRIC is a welcoming arts and wellness series designed for adults 55+ to foster creativity\, connection\, and well-being. Hosted by SAIVA at Lackawanna Station in Montclair\, this program brings the community together through engaging\, beginner-friendly experiences. By engaging this audience\, the project preserves cultural heritage\, strengthens social networks\, and contributes to overall well-being\, aligning directly with Essex County’s commitment to arts\, culture\, and community enrichment. \nParticipants can enjoy: \nGentle chair yoga and meditation sessions to support relaxation and mobility \nCreative art sessions that encourage self-expression \nA warm\, social environment focused on building meaningful connections \n✨ Session Dates: \nChair Yoga & Meditation at 11AM-12PM: May 20\, July 22\, September 23 \nArt Sessions 2-3pm: June 17\, August 19 \n🎟️ Registration required | Limited to 20 participants per session \nNo prior experience is needed. Each session is designed to be accessible\, inclusive\, and enriching. \nFor Wellness Sessions: \nTake a deep breath… and give your body the gentle care it deserves. \nThis welcoming chair yoga and meditation class is thoughtfully designed for seniors who want to feel stronger\, more relaxed\, and more at ease in their bodies—without getting down on the floor or pushing beyond their limits. Using a sturdy chair for support\, you’ll move through simple\, low-impact stretches and guided breathing that help improve flexibility\, balance\, and overall mobility in a safe and accessible way. \nResearch shows that chair yoga can enhance strength\, reduce joint pain and stiffness\, and even improve balance and confidence with movement—helping to lower the risk of falls while supporting everyday activities. \nBut this class is about more than movement… it’s about how you feel. \nThrough gentle meditation and calming breathwork\, you’ll learn simple tools to manage stress\, quiet the mind\, and reconnect with a sense of inner calm. These practices activate the body’s natural relaxation response\, helping to reduce anxiety\, improve mood\, and support better sleep. \nYou’ll leave each session feeling: \n• More grounded and centered \n• Gently stretched and energized \n• Mentally clear and relaxed \nNo experience is needed—just come as you are. Every movement can be modified\, and you are always encouraged to go at your own pace. \nThis is a supportive\, feel-good environment where you can move\, breathe\, and connect—not just with your body\, but with a sense of calm\, stability\, and well-being that carries into your everyday life. \nBecause it’s never too late to feel better in your body… and more at peace in your mind. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
URL:https://montclairlocal.news/event/fabric-arts-and-wellness-series-at-lackawanna-station/2026-05-20/
LOCATION:Lackawanna Plaza Montclair\, NJ\, Lackawanna Plaza\, Montclair\, NJ\, 07042\, United States
CATEGORIES:Art & Culture,Community,General Events,Health & Wellness
